   imageUrl="Macro-detail, three-quarter off-axis view of Carl Jung’s hand holding an oxidized-metal pipe in the immediate foreground, captured with a macro-flat-field lens. Selective focus isolates the etched textures of the pipe against a deep bokeh degradation of a museum-clinical library. Surfaces exhibit the materiality of bone-ivory skin, pigment-fresco walls, and dry-stone shelving. Specular museum-led lighting carves high-contrast edges across the subject, rendered in a mineral-cool palette with a restrained bleach-bypass finish. The asymmetric composition utilizes an edge-crop, emphasizing the tactile evidence of age and historical materials through digital medium-format clarity. Strict exclusions (do not generate): sparkles, glitter, ungrounded floating embers, magical glowing glyphs, sci-fi energy effects, theatrical artificial fog, mystical floating dust rays, monochromatic sepia wash, aged yellow tint filter. Maintain photographic material realism and physical optical discipline." /%}
